cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use neuroconsumer, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "neuroconsumer: Controlled Visual Experimentation in Consumer Research"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
authors:
  - family-names: "Sánchez-Núñez"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7845-9506"
url: "https://pablosancheznunez.com/neuroconsumer/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablosancheznunez/neuroconsumer"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - consumer research
  - advertising research
  - visual stimuli
  - experimental design
  - eye tracking
  - areas of interest
  - neuromarketing
  - R
abstract: >-
  An R package for constructing, manipulating, validating and documenting
  visual stimuli in consumer research and advertising studies: declarative
  experimental factors, deterministic SVG/PNG rendering, Areas of Interest
  with persistent identifiers, and verification that conditions differ only
  in the declared dimensions.
